  "narrative": {
    "text": "**Business & market dynamics:** Health Catalyst is navigating a platform migration that is pressuring top-line growth and creating duplicate hosting costs, contributing to a year-over-year revenue decline. However, the most recent quarter showed a revenue beat versus guidance, suggesting some stabilization. Demand indicators include heavy data-loading work for health information exchange client deployments, though this also weighs on near-term technology margins. The broader narrative is one of transition: the business is absorbing the costs of moving clients to a new platform while aiming to preserve and eventually improve profitability.\n\n**Management strategy and execution:** Management is pursuing an explicit margin focus and has initiated a strategic review, signaling a willingness to evaluate the business structure. After a previous quarter’s guidance that came in below expectations, they delivered results above the high end of their own forecast in the latest period, which may help rebuild credibility. Executives highlighted year-over-year adjusted gross margin improvement despite migration-related friction, and they appear to be balancing cost discipline with the operational demands of the platform shift. The strategic review adds an element of potential change to the execution story.",
